  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Now plotting the diagram we get,</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0074_1f77fcf3017b.png\" style=\"width: 317px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>: area of shaded region as shown in the above figure,</p><p>Shaded portion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> circular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mo>Ar</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Hence, Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, plotting the diagram of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>min</mi><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msqrt><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0074_c5cf65e29be3.png\" style=\"width: 310px; height: 200px;\" /></p><p>Area of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>: area of shaded region as shown in the above figure,</p><p>Area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Ar</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></math>&nbsp;Area of arc of circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>area</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mrow><mtext>area</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>o</mi><mi>f</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
